WEBVTT

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.370
<b>Is Tokyo Governor Inagi Involved in Terrorism?!</b>

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.760
Didn't you save the life of 
Kobari-san's daughter?

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.480
Madoka looked into it for me.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.750
And the way you panicked 
when the autopsy video played

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.370
wasn't like you.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.590
Do you regret what happened 
with Naganuma-san?

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.570
Chinju-san, was it?

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.510
What will you do now?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.760
I will follow Inagi-sensei. That is all.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:39.930
I see.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.520
Tell me one last thing.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.320
Was it your ideal to control Tokyo?

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.270
Or did you just want to make an ideal city?

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.440
Control?

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.250
Never.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.530
I was just in too much of a hurry.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.720
I see... All right.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.240
Then I'll go

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.040
protect the future you tried 
to create, Inagi-san.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.960
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.330
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.430
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.810
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.090
<b>File 12: Wonderful Days</b>

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:41.740
Did you see the news?

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.240
I heard they arrested the governor.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.100
I can't believe it!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.430
<b>Takao</b>

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.470
I heard rumors that were 
basically urban legends,

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.350
but I didn't expect anything to happen 
before the City Summit ended.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.660
What happened with the City Summit?

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.750
The lieutenant governor took 
over, and it's still on.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.020
But they moved it to Sapporo, right?

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.910
Why Sapporo?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.540
Huh?!

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.310
Is that true, Prime Minister?

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.550
Yes.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.890
We've learned that the space elevator

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.740
is loaded with Image Master.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.340
Image Master is

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.720
the type of explosive used in 
the Rudra incident, right?

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.160
Yes. It seems the previous administration

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.580
covertly acquired them from Carupanuba

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.800
and placed them on the satellite 
as a strategic defense weapon.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.110
It was developed as a satellite weapon?

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.140
Does the rest of the world know?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.150
But we don't need to worry now, right?

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.440
Bird severed the cable linking it to Earth,

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.640
and it's leaving geostationary orbit.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.690
If we leave it, it'll float off.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.900
No, the satellite and the Image 
Master will fall on Tokyo.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:41.880
No way!

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.830
On Tokyo?

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.990
How bad will the damage be?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.490
The association has run the 
calculations many times,

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.950
and the results are disastrous.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.380
Within five days, the satellite that 
forms the space elevator's base

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.620
will enter the atmosphere.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:59.380
<b>Takao</b>

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.820
The damage from the Image Master will spread

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:59.380
to Saitama, Kanagawa, Chiba, and Shizuoka.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.840
Former Governor Inagi tried to avoid this, but...

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.280
Well, Kyoukai-kun?

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.050
I agree with you, Kyoukai-sama.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.350
There's only one way to stop 
Tokyo from being destroyed.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.180
Directly activate the emergency 
switch on the satellite,

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.270
causing it to leave Earth's gravitational field.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.160
So that's the only way after all?

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:20.760
Everyone...

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.460
Bird is causing the satellite to accelerate.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.910
There's no time to send an astronaut.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.040
The association has decided that

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.120
using Willwears is the only 
solution to this problem.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.500
Using Willwears in space?

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:39.590
I now propose the formation of a special 
joint government-civilian task force!

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.590
Is that all right, Prime Minister?

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.780
Well, um...

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.550
I'll have to take the plan back with me.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.010
What about the USDF's operation?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.400
No problem.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.380
Prime Minister!

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.600
Very well, then...

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:54.740
Good.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.900
We will now act to protect 
our citizens and our country!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.750
Right!

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.710
What?! The prime minister's 
residence is moving to Fukuoka?

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.210
Without giving evacuation orders?

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.280
I'm sure they had their reasons, 
even if it may not look like it.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.940
So, what's the plan?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:17.540
They're sending one unit from the 
Third Mobile and one from the USDF.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:18.830
Just two units?

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.460
They're worried about the damage if 
anything happens in low-Earth orbit,

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.100
so they'll handle it in medium-Earth orbit.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.300
Given the time we have and tools at 
our disposal, it's the best we can do.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:34.560
The USDF will use a plane to carry 
the Willwear to high altitude,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.690
and then launch it.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.270
Of course, I'll be the one going to space.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:39.480
Miho...

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.980
I think we'll all be working together 
to launch one person.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.360
Here, from the new city hall.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.920
Kyoukai-san, are you there?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.070
I sure am.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.200
How will they get back?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.780
No need to worry about that.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.160
They can use the satellite's emergency unit.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.670
Oh, that's perfect.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:57.890
Right, Brain?

00:05:58.600 --> 00:05:59.530
Yeah...

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:01.590
Kyoukai-kun, just tell us already.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.630
How likely is this to succeed?

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.720
Bird's causing the satellite 
to continually accelerate,

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.590
so the odds are about 31%.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:11.650
I thought so.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:12.610
You thought so?

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.670
Torigoe, that's why you're a failure as a person.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.330
Use Willwears to reach the rendezvous point,

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.460
work in space for the first time,

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.850
and then attempt atmospheric reentry.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.530
There's no way...

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.740
Um, who's going to space?

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.320
I'm the chief. I'll go.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.780
No, I'll go.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.410
Unfortunately, neither of you qualifies.

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:39.450
In addition to mass, air tightness, 
and environmental protection,

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.640
there's the need to supply 
nutrients and oxygen,

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.910
as well as the required 
thruster modifications.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.690
Only two Willwears qualify.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:49.380
Oscar II, the Strike Interceptor,

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.640
and Oscar VI, the Fine Familia.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.350
I'll go!

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:56.780
Kuroki-kun...

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.560
Asami will get cocky if she succeeds, 
so it's best not to let her.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.110
And...

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:04.420
It was his failures that caused this.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.350
That's why I need to handle it.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.440
So, everyone, back me up!

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:10.110
Right!

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.530
Everyone, let's all work together...

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:15.800
Boss!

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.490
Director...

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.580
I brought what you requested, scumwad d**k.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:20.800
Scum—

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:22.380
Thank you.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:23.880
We'll handle the rest.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.290
Once you've got it unloaded, 
go back to Nagoya.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.630
It may be dangerous here.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:32.060
Shove it up your ass, pencil d**k.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.300
We're all here to help your wh*re-eating ass.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.970
Hear that, slaves?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.020
Yes, boss!

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.300
Thank you, everyone.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.730
I'm amazed you know what they're saying.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:43.650
Huh?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.900
Madoka-san, what are you doing here?

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.570
I want to do something, too.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.470
Thanks.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.870
We don't have enough people, 
so I'll take you up on that.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.030
Madoka-chan and everyone from Senars, Inc.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:54.660
Yes.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:57.770
I see...

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.090
Knowing Bird, he may wait 
until the last minute.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.250
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:02.960
Not bad.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.250
I'm so frustrated with myself.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:09.490
I was so close to him, and I didn't notice a thing.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.470
Hey, more importantly, isn't there another?

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:13.930
Another?

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.590
With him.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.830
Why won't you let me get to city hall?

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:27.400
Why did you suddenly move 
the summit to Sapporo?

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.960
You're so amazing, Emilia-san.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.650
What are you talking about?

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:35.590
Even though you're using the 
Centaur Unit for this mission,

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:36.620
you're still calm.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.450
That's not true.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.250
I still feel like I'm going to 
choke every time I see it.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.770
Then why?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.080
The boss said you're not technically part 
of the unit, so you don't have to do it.

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:49.900
I owe Kuroki-san a debt.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.550
So, until he comes back, I won't run.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.260
You won't run...

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.440
All right.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.260
I'll do my best, too!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.350
I think it's all right to take your time with that.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.310
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.980
It's been a while, Madoka-chan. 
Will you be okay?

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.940
Yes, no problem.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:11.780
Huh?

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.490
Haruka-san, did you connect the 
system to an Internet auction?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:16.900
Oh, well...

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:20.070
The time limit runs out right when 
Kuroki-san is supposed to come back.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:22.440
I figured it'd be a good way to kill time.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.970
You're worried, aren't you?

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:25.460
Am I?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.920
Maybe I am.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.960
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.050
D*ckhead!

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.230
Oh, yeah!

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.320
D*ckhead!

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.530
Oh, yeah!

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:35.670
D*ckhead!

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.900
Oh, yeah!

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.070
D*ckhead!

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.530
Oh, yeah!

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.100
Hey, boss!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.950
No worries, no problems.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:47.400
By tomorrow, Space Kuroki ready go!

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:48.750
Thank you, director.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:50.090
You're a wonderful person!

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:52.590
And you've grown up into a 
wonderful piece of shit!

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:53.440
I have not.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.160
Kazari-kun, may I borrow that checker?

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.410
Kazari-kun?

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:00.840
Funasaka-san...

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.360
In Osaka, I thought I was finally grown up.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.250
But I'm still no good.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.430
Why do you think that?

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:09.800
When Kyoukai-sama said

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:12.980
either I or Kuroki-san had to go to space,

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.070
I realized I didn't want to go...

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:16.720
That's normal.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.470
But Kuroki-san...

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.590
I'm an idiot!

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:23.220
I was arrogant because I was part of the elite!

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:25.390
Brain...

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:28.070
But we weren't good enough.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.190
I'm sorry...

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.550
There's a soba place I always go to.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:35.570
In Chindaiji.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.400
Once Kuroki-kun comes back 
from space, let's all go.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.170
It's great to drink

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.780
in the middle of the day at a soba place.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:49.020
<i>My splendid, splendid prince, 
the most wonderful man in the world!</i>

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.960
<i>How about this place?</i>

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.470
Thank you, Liko-chan.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.920
I'll keep it in mind.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.340
That's amazing.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:00.850
At this point, I can't say anything 
but, "That's amazing."

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.500
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.680
That's also amazing.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.770
Hey, where's Kuroki-kun?

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.950
I want to measure his center of mass.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.860
You can't just come in here.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.730
This place is off-limits right now.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.340
If you wanted to talk, Komieri-chan,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.300
I would have come to you.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.910
That would cause a huge fuss.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:21.570
Why?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.910
I may not be the right person to say it,

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.660
but people are bashing you due to your 
relationship with the governor, Kuroki-kun.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:29.310
I see.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.130
If I get fired, will your office hire me?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:34.650
What are you talking about?

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.780
Anyway, what's going on?

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.830
The government's acting really strange.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.020
All the embassies are—

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:44.900
I'll explain when I get back from 
my business trip, okay?

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:45.550
Business trip?

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.410
Yeah.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.370
When I get back, I'll have the 
scoop of a lifetime for you.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.450
A scoop?

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:50.760
A scoop, huh?

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.070
<b>Souichiro-san 

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.030
What do you want at this point?

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.520
I thought I should call you.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.820
You're worried about me?

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.050
I suppose.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.500
But I'm worried about someone else more.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:17.140
He's not like you. Sometimes he 
does incredibly risky things.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.290
He may be a lazy boor,

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.170
but he's a co-worker.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:21.990
If anything happens—

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:24.570
You don't need to tell me! That's my mission!

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.690
And... And...

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.630
Sorry... What was that?

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:31.500
Huh?

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:34.440
Oh, jeez... I hate calling back.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.160
Yes, this is Kuroki.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.400
What? What's up?

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.360
Who?

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.500
Hinata-chan, who are you putting on?

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.370
Me.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:46.070
Oh, that's rare.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:49.280
I heard you're going into space?

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.880
What, are you worried about me?

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:52.750
Not really.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.180
I'll be back soon.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.300
Once this is all over,

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:59.340
we've decided we'll all go 
look for your little sister.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:02.600
Madoka and Hayashida-san say they'll help.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:05.620
Bye.

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:06.400
Wait...

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:08.190
There's something I have to tell you.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.410
What? Just tell me already.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.690
We will now begin the mission.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.190
Willwear unit, equip immediately.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:21.870
Right!

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.120
Inner unit, begin output.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.500
Oscar Series, set units.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.510
All units, to your positions!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.420
We'll stand by in the sky.

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.220
Oscar VII, you all right?

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.190
I'm fine. Ready to go.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.630
How is the Falcon Unit that left first?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:06.030
It successfully separated from the rocket.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.940
It should make target altitude.

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:10.720
Group-pissing closet pervs, go, go, go!

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.740
Would you please calm down, director?

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:15.080
Oh, power harassment...

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:17.340
Tokyo catapult, setup complete.

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:18.420
It's ready to go anytime.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.220
This is Oscar II.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:20.920
Ready to go!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.090
Let's get started, then.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.250
Drawn-Sword Mode!

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.340
<b>Oscar IV, Koutetsujin Nanakamado Unit</b>

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:26.340
Oscar II.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:27.220
Launch!

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.090
Launch.

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:29.300
Launch!

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.260
<b>Oscar V, Primavera Pantera Unit</b>

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:32.930
Apprehend.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:40.560
Folk Dance Field!

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.560
<b>Oscar VI Accessory 
Prod Familia Series</b>

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:42.940
Altitude has broken 20,000 meters.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:45.260
Kick Dash Iota!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:47.610
<b>Oscar VI, Fine Familia Unit</b>

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.170
Complete Edition!

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.410
Sending Oscar II's information.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.370
Oscar III, take over joint control.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.370
<b>Oscar VII, Foundation Omega Unit</b>

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.830
Roger, Oscar VII.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.830
<b>Oscar III, Metistructure Ibuki Unit</b>

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.910
Joint control set.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:14:59.160
<b>Connection Complete</b>

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.040
As planned, the USDF is going ahead.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.960
I'll be going on ahead,

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.170
<b>USDF, Senshin</b>

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.630
police and civilians.

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:05.750
Oscar I!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:07.670
<b>Oscar I, Elf Sigma Unit</b>

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.670
I'm aware, Oscar II.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.300
Let's do this, partner!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:08.880
<b>Oscar II, Strike Interceptor Unit</b>

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.430
Yeah, I'll let you handle the rest.

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:12.300
Bye.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.000
It succeeded.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.590
We'll reach target altitude in—

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:21.440
Something appeared at target altitude!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.270
It can't be!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:26.980
What?!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.620
Oscar II, keep going!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.780
You're following us all the way up here?!

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.330
S-Souichirou...

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:41.900
Don't worry about it.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.840
He'll be able to handle it by himself.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:56.710
It's been about 48 hours since 
they started taking action.

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:59.060
How long will they struggle?

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:00.270
Hey...

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:05.400
Are you planning on staying in Tokyo 
until the explosives fall?

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:08.260
Waiting until the last second 
is more fun, isn't it?

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:09.610
More importantly,

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:13.540
can you do something about that 
stupid shoplifting habit of yours?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:14.530
You caught me, huh?

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:19.720
I'll be on my way to the next 
country to prepare things.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.150
Yeah, thanks.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.270
See you.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:50.070
Congratulations.

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:53.280
Looks like you reached your destination.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:55.270
This is Oscar II.

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:57.000
I'm about to begin the mission.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.350
Any irregularities?

00:16:58.350 --> 00:16:59.810
Don't worry.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.370
Everything has gone according to plan.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.580
Good...

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:07.270
Okay, I'm opening the rocket's control panel!

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:14.550
Uh-oh... You opened Pandora's box.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.890
Unfortunately, I didn't put any hope inside.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.940
No way... You're telling us this now?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.770
<b>Hakata-Tenjin</b>

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.770
The report from the office was late.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:33.370
The rocket was still in Tanegashima.

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:35.740
Instead, unmanned Willwears were there.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.490
They just now showed up.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.130
You know, this is

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:42.450
that Hachijou guy's fault.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.360
It appears the plan is going well.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:45.890
Can you do something?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.210
Can we do something?

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:50.880
Wait, you're kidding me!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.550
What the hell?!

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:02.430
Destructive Ram Cannon, fire!

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:07.630
Target for destruction: Strike Interceptor.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:08.980
Damn it!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.060
What am I supposed to do with these?!

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:13.570
Destroying.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.240
Kuroki-san!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.200
Kuroki!

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.370
Kyoukai-sama, we'll have to use it!

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.740
Yes, we already told Kuroki-kun, too.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.450
There's something you can use?

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:26.150
A special function the association 
built on its own.

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:28.080
So it's a secret from the government.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:30.290
<b>Hakata-Tenjin</b>

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:30.290
You can't use that!

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.410
Who cares?!

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.880
Give your authorization, Prime Minister!

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.340
Ah, y-yes...

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.800
Right, authorization received.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:36.760
Confirming authorization.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:38.340
I authorize it!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.150
Roger.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:40.960
Can you hear me, Oscar II?

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.580
Yeah, thanks!

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.810
Change mode to Complete
Annihilation Ram Function!

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.500
Unlocking Susanoo.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.400
Behold the association's knowledge!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.990
So you have that?

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:58.790
Inagi-san, I'm doing my best trick.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:02.950
Frontal Punch!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.960
Wow!

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:12.380
Hey, hey! No point in running, asshole!

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.520
Wait, are these the explosives?

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.350
Now, what will you do?

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.030
The Strike can only fight at close range, right?

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:26.510
But if you attack and the Image Master blows,

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:28.060
what will happen to you?

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.520
I'll either get caught in the explosion and die

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.940
or get blown into space.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:35.520
I guess it doesn't matter which.

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:38.990
The emergency rocket wasn't here.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.950
So either way, I have to blow it up here.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:42.790
Kuroki-san!

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:43.570
Kuroki-kun!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:47.290
And the Susanoo eats up 
a hell of a lot of battery.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:50.120
Even if I make it, I only have 
another five minutes...

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.290
Bye.

00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:54.500
I'm grateful to all of you!

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.590
D-Don't give me that!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.190
What about the change you owe 
me from yesterday's drinks?!

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:00.790
And the blue cheese—

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:03.270
Sorry, blockhead.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:05.570
The way you're always so dense, I...

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.140
Well, never mind.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.440
Kuroki!

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:30.420
<i>So Kuroki will receive a posthumous promotion</i>

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.080
<i>to senior supervisor?</i>

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:36.800
<i>But if you die, you have nothing left.</i>

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.130
Boss!

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.490
You're late, pencil d**k!

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:41.130
I'll jerk you off, shitface!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:43.840
Director, I don't think that outfit 
is appropriate for a funeral.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.000
My, what a thing to say.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.430
It's not a funeral.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.770
Sorry, I'm late!

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:50.700
How?

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.100
The lazy boor...

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.310
I figured you'd be the one 
guy who hadn't heard.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:57.140
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.480
Well, Jirou called me...

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:01.910
I discussed this with Yamabuki-kun,

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:06.990
but there's a chance that Bird has set 
a trap on the space elevator's base.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.920
Separate the return unit first,

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.520
and leave it at a different point.

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.910
So I used the last of my battery to 
shield myself from the explosion

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:17.550
and moved to the unit.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.210
Jirou's sure handy to have around, huh?

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:24.020
W-Wait, where's Bird, then?

00:21:24.020 --> 00:21:25.540
You didn't hear about that, either?

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.370
It's been a long time, Senpai.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.690
I'm afraid you've landed at Yokota Base.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:35.100
I tampered with the autopilot.

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:38.980
Are you happy to have friends now, Mythos?

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.530
You had them too, right?

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:47.000
We followed your friend

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.980
to find you.

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.160
Her code name is "A-ko."

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:54.530
Do you remember when I suggested 
that there might be a Monkey?

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.470
I can't believe you went with "Ape."

00:21:56.470 --> 00:21:57.350
Senpai...

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:01.140
What was I to you?

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:02.780
What are you talking about?

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.710
You were an irreplaceable part.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:05.550
I see.

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:08.430
Thank you for your answer!

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.640
So that's what happened!

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:16.620
O-Oh...

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:19.100
And this "Ape"?

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:21.620
We'll deal with that later.

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:23.320
For now...

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:27.530
<b>Celebrating Inspector Kuroki's Safe Return</b>

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:24.970
It's our special guest!

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:27.530
Today's special guest is back!

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:28.740
Kuroki-san!

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:31.150
Everyone, let's say it together!

00:22:31.490 --> 00:22:32.990
Ready...

00:22:32.990 --> 00:22:35.530
Welcome back!

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<b>Funeral Incense</b>

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:39.080
Good work.
